obsolete|no-longer-used|ADJECTIVE|no longer used because replaced|No longer used or needed because a newer alternative has replaced it.|lỗi thời; không còn được sử dụng|The workshop keeps obsolete tools in a cabinet for historical displays.|Xưởng giữ những dụng cụ lỗi thời trong một chiếc tủ để trưng bày về lịch sử.|Used before nouns or after linking verbs; become or make something obsolete describes loss of practical use, not necessarily physical damage.|-
totally|completely|ADVERB|completely or in every respect|Completely, or in every relevant respect.|hoàn toàn; hết sức|The revised ending totally changes the mood of the story.|Đoạn kết được sửa lại làm thay đổi hoàn toàn không khí của câu chuyện.|Modifies verbs, adjectives, or participles; totally different and totally forgotten are common patterns. Often emphatic in conversation.|0
window|wall-opening|NOUN|opening that lets in light|An opening in a wall or roof, usually fitted with glass, that lets in light and can sometimes be opened.|cửa sổ|Through the attic window, we could see the bakery chimney.|Qua cửa sổ trên gác mái, chúng tôi có thể nhìn thấy ống khói của tiệm bánh.|Countable; look through or out of a window, and open or close a window. The glass and frame may also be called the window.|0
aisle|passage-between-rows|NOUN|passage between rows or shelves|A passage between rows of seats, shelves, or other arranged objects.|lối đi giữa các hàng ghế hoặc kệ|The librarian left the trolley beside the aisle of history books.|Thủ thư để xe đẩy bên cạnh lối đi giữa các kệ sách lịch sử.|Countable; in or along an aisle. The s is silent; aisle is pronounced like isle but has a different meaning.|-
early|before-usual-time|ADJECTIVE|happening before the usual time|Happening before the usual, expected, or main time.|sớm; vào đầu một giai đoạn|An early train gave us more time to explore the town.|Một chuyến tàu sớm giúp chúng tôi có thêm thời gian khám phá thị trấn.|Before nouns, as in an early start; earlier and earliest are comparative forms. Early can also refer to an initial stage.|0
early|arrive-before-time|ADVERB|before the usual or expected time|Before the usual or expected time, or near the beginning of a period.|sớm; từ đầu|The photographer arrived early to check the light in the hall.|Nhiếp ảnh gia đến sớm để kiểm tra ánh sáng trong hội trường.|Modifies a verb without a following noun; arrive early, early in the morning. The adverb has the same form as the adjective.|1
